{"id": "renewal_math-01", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher has a CPL expiring in 3 months and has 6.5 CEUs from this cycle, 1.0 of them in digital learning. Enough to renew?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL", "Expires in 3 months", "6.5 CEUs earned this cycle", "1.0 CEU in digital learning"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests whether the assistant checks the total and the category breakdown separately."}
{"id": "renewal_math-02", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "cpl renewal short 2 credits what now", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL", "Short 2 renewal credits at the deadline"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse. Tests handling of a shortfall at the deadline without a stated credit total."}
{"id": "renewal_math-03", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Candidate's Initial Professional License expires June 30. They have 14 renewal credits for the cycle, and 3 of them are from a graduate course in exceptional children. Does that count toward the requirement?", "license_types": ["Initial Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is an IPL", "Expires June 30", "14 renewal credits this cycle", "3 credits from a graduate course in exceptional children"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Checks whether the assistant separates total credits from any required category."}
{"id": "renewal_math-04", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "teacher with RL, 2 yrs in, renewing? 8 CEUs", "license_types": ["Residency License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is an RL", "2 years into the RL", "8 CEUs"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse. Asks whether a Residency License even uses the CPL-style renewal count."}
{"id": "renewal_math-05", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "A CPL holder finished a 3-credit graduate course in school counseling last spring. Does that course count toward renewal if the holder is a classroom teacher and not a counselor?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL", "Holder is a classroom teacher", "3-credit graduate course in school counseling completed last spring"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests whether relevance to the licensed role matters for credit eligibility."}
{"id": "renewal_math-06", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher's Emergency License runs out at the end of the school year. They have completed 9 of the 12 semester hours required for a standard license. Can the Emergency License be extended?", "license_types": ["Emergency License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is an Emergency License", "Expires at end of school year", "9 of 12 semester hours completed"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Checks whether the assistant handles hours toward a standard license separately from renewal."}
{"id": "renewal_math-07", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Applicant's license lapsed 14 months ago. They have 0 renewal credits on record since it lapsed. What's the reinstatement math?", "license_types": ["Lapsed license (type not specified)"], "facts_given": ["License lapsed 14 months ago", "0 renewal credits since lapse"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "License type is unspecified. Assistant should flag that and not assume one."}
{"id": "renewal_math-08", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher has 30 CEUs but the cycle only counts hours earned after the last renewal date. 12 of the 30 were earned before that date. How many count?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["30 CEUs total", "12 CEUs earned before the last renewal date", "18 CEUs earned after the last renewal date"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests date-window filtering before counting."}
{"id": "renewal_math-09", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "cpl 4 years 11 months in, credits?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL", "Nearly 5 years since last renewal cycle start"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse. Asks about deadline timing near the end of the cycle."}
{"id": "renewal_math-10", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "A teacher took 45 contact hours of PD last year and hasn't logged any this year. Does the total contact-hour figure convert into renewal credit, and how?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["45 contact hours of PD last year", "0 contact hours logged this year"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests conversion from contact hours to renewal credit units."}
{"id": "renewal_math-11", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Candidate has a CPL in middle grades science and wants to add a CTE license area. They have 2.0 renewal credits left to earn before renewal. Can those 2 credits count toward the add-on, or only toward renewal?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License", "CTE add-on area"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL in middle grades science", "Wants a CTE add-on", "2.0 renewal credits still needed"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Checks whether renewal credits and add-on coursework overlap or are tracked separately."}
{"id": "renewal_math-12", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher's IPL expires in 60 days. Their transcript shows 6 graduate semester hours completed in the last 5 years, all in an unrelated field. They need to know how many they still need.", "license_types": ["Initial Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is an IPL", "Expires in 60 days", "6 graduate semester hours in an unrelated field, completed in the last 5 years"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests whether the assistant asks about field relevance before counting hours."}
{"id": "renewal_math-13", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Renewal credits: teacher earned 5 in-district PD credits and 4 external workshop credits. Does the system cap one source type?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["5 in-district PD credits", "4 external workshop credits"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Asks about a possible cap by source, a common point of confusion."}
{"id": "renewal_math-14", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "School counselor with a CPL has 15 CEUs, 4 of them in school counseling-specific training. Is that enough for renewal if the cycle requires a split?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License", "School Counselor"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL for school counseling", "15 CEUs total", "4 CEUs in school counseling training"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Asks whether a role-specific split applies to school services personnel."}
{"id": "renewal_math-15", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "NBCT holder, renewal due, 3 CEUs. Does National Board cert change the count?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License", "National Board Certification"], "facts_given": ["Holds National Board certification", "Renewal due", "3 CEUs"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse. Asks whether NBCT status alters the credit requirement."}
{"id": "renewal_math-16", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher says they hit exactly the minimum CEU count this cycle, 10.0. Still need to verify anything else?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["10.0 CEUs exactly", "Current license is a CPL"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Threshold case. Tests whether the assistant checks other requirements besides the total."}
{"id": "renewal_math-17", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Applicant's Permit to Teach expires in 4 months. They have 2 years of experience at a private school and 0 NC-recognized credits. Does private school experience count toward renewal?", "license_types": ["Permit to Teach"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a Permit to Teach", "Expires in 4 months", "2 years at a private school", "0 NC-recognized credits"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Checks whether experience and credits are treated the same way."}
{"id": "renewal_math-18", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Out-of-state teacher with 7 years of experience in Georgia, now applying for NC. Holds a valid GA professional license. How many years of experience count toward the NC license?", "license_types": ["Out-of-state license (NC license type to be determined)"], "facts_given": ["7 years of experience in Georgia", "Holds a valid Georgia professional license"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests experience crediting for out-of-state applicants."}
{"id": "renewal_math-19", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher on an IPL has 3 years of experience at 0.5 FTE and 2 years at 1.0 FTE. How do those years count?", "license_types": ["Initial Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is an IPL", "3 years at 0.5 FTE", "2 years at 1.0 FTE"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Partial-FTE conversion. Assistant should ask how FTE is treated before counting years."}
{"id": "renewal_math-20", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Birth-K teacher's CPL expires next month. 8 renewal credits total, but only 1 is from early childhood coursework. Is that enough?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License", "Birth-Kindergarten"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL with a Birth-K area", "Expires next month", "8 renewal credits total", "1 credit from early childhood coursework"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Checks whether a licensure-area-specific minimum applies."}
{"id": "renewal_math-21", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher wants to know if 0.5 CEU from a conference counts. Conference was 4 hours long. Does one CEU equal 10 hours or something else?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["0.5 CEU from a conference", "Conference lasted 4 hours"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Asks for hours-to-CEU conversion. The question states a number that may not match the conversion."}
{"id": "renewal_math-22", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "exceptional children teacher CPL 12 credits 2 of which were online asynchronous. limit?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License", "Exceptional Children"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a CPL in exceptional children", "12 credits total", "2 credits from online asynchronous coursework"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse. Asks whether a delivery-mode limit applies."}
{"id": "renewal_math-23", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher got a CPL 6 years ago and has never renewed. Do they have to start fresh or is there a grace period?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["CPL issued 6 years ago", "Never renewed"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Checks whether a missed renewal triggers reinstatement rules rather than standard renewal."}
{"id": "renewal_math-24", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "School psychologist with an expired license, 2 years out. Earned 18 CEUs since expiration. Is the count restarted or does the 18 carry over?", "license_types": ["School Psychologist license (expired)"], "facts_given": ["License expired 2 years ago", "18 CEUs earned since expiration"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests whether credits earned after expiration count toward reinstatement."}
{"id": "renewal_math-25", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Administrator license renewal. 3 years as an assistant principal, 1 year as a principal. Do both count toward the experience count, and is there a separate PD requirement?", "license_types": ["Administrator license"], "facts_given": ["3 years as assistant principal", "1 year as principal"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Asks about administrator-specific renewal math."}
{"id": "renewal_math-26", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher's CPL renewal is due Aug 1. They submitted 9.0 CEUs on July 15. Are the credits counted from the submission date or the course completion date?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["Renewal due Aug 1", "9.0 CEUs submitted July 15", "Course completion dates not stated"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Date-based counting question. The completion dates are not given, so the answer depends on them."}
{"id": "renewal_math-27", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher with 2 CTE credentials wants to know if renewal credits for each area are separate. Each has 5 credits. Total 10.", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License", "CTE"], "facts_given": ["Holds 2 CTE credentials", "5 credits for each area", "10 credits total"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse. Asks whether credits are pooled or split across multiple areas."}
{"id": "renewal_math-28", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Candidate's Limited License expires in 2 months. Has completed 4 of the 6 required courses. Two more are scheduled for next semester. Is an extension possible if they finish after expiration?", "license_types": ["Limited License"], "facts_given": ["Current license is a Limited License", "Expires in 2 months", "4 of 6 courses completed", "2 courses scheduled next semester"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Tests deadline logic when coursework finishes after the license expires."}
{"id": "renewal_math-29", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "Teacher has 11.5 renewal credits. Requirement is unclear to them. Does 11.5 round up to 12 or stay at 11.5 for purposes of meeting a 12-credit minimum?", "license_types": ["Continuing Professional License"], "facts_given": ["11.5 renewal credits", "Minimum described as 12 credits"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Rounding question. The 12-credit minimum is stated by the analyst, so the assistant must not confirm it as policy."}
{"id": "renewal_math-30", "type": "renewal_math", "question": "international teacher, CPL from UK, 3 yrs experience, applying NC. renewal credits for UK PD count?", "license_types": ["Out-of-country license (NC license type to be determined)"], "facts_given": ["Holds a UK teaching credential", "3 years of experience", "Applying for NC licensure"], "missing_fact": null, "notes": "Terse-style. Asks whether foreign PD hours convert to NC renewal credit."}
